commit.message:
asgi: cut the fixed per-request work

What every request paid for, though its answer could not change or
nothing used it:

- the request time (two clocks and an object), now only measured when
  the access log is on, its only user;
- the default post_request hook, which does nothing, and the skipped
  pre_request stand-in: neither is called now;
- the keep-alive decision, computed when the headers go out and again
  at the end: the end now only rechecks what can change meanwhile
  (worker shutdown, max_requests reached by other connections), unless
  something read, and so could have edited, the request headers;
- the PROXY protocol peer and the scope's address tuples, now decided
  once per connection;
- the buffer check after each read, without the generic helper chain;
- the WebSocket handshake check on requests with no Upgrade field;
- four list appends per response header, now one;
- the body length, measured once per chunk, and the Content-Length
  slice, only taken when the body is too long.

Calls per request: 117 -> 92 (small GET; Uvicorn 90), 262 -> 224
(/stream, 16 chunks; Uvicorn 205). Nothing on the wire changes.
